oracle: subset definition (LANG84 phase 7a: an int outside i64 traps Trap.Overflow; CPython would make a bigger int). Host CPython 3.11.17, 3.12.3, 3.13.16 print the stdout before `trap:` and then 9.223372036854776e+18, the float of 9223372036854775808, outside i64 before the conversion
command: {python3.11,python3.12,python3.13} -I overflow_inside_float.py
result (host): exit 0; stdout starts with the part of <name>.expect before `trap:`, then a float
releases: 3.11.17, 3.12.3 and 3.13.16 by their own host interpreters (above); 3.5.10, 3.6.0 and 3.16.0a1 through the py3 profile's pinned-source evidence (python-iir-compiler/src/profiles.rs)
why: the int sub-expression overflows i64 before it meets the float, so it traps instead of promoting to a bignum (stated divergence)
